<title>USA: Grubb Q4 oper shr $0.26 vs $0.01.</title>
<headline>Grubb Q4 oper shr $0.26 vs $0.01.</headline>
<dateline>NORTHBROOK, Ill. 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In thousands of dollars except percentages and per</p>
<p>share data)</p>
<p>			   Three Months Ended   Twelve Months Ended</p>
<p>				    June 30,		 June 30,</p>
<p>				1997	1996	1997     1996</p>
<p>    Total revenue	60,076     49,052    228,630   193,728</p>
<p>    Net income	    8,457	1,290     19,010     2,102</p>
<p>    EPS (fully diluted) 0.38	 0.06	 0.93     (0.10)</p>
<p>Net income before non-</p>
<p>  recurring items(a)    5,866	  862     12,840     1,640</p>
<p>EPS before non-recurring</p>
<p>     items (fully diluted)0.26	0.01	0.63	(0.13)</p>
<p>NOTE: (a) Non-recurring items consist of the Company's deferred tax benefit, special charges, unusual items, and extraordinary items, including the elimination of long-term debt. Both the fiscal year and fourth quarter include a $3.2 million tax-deferred benefit. Full company name is Grubb &amp; Ellis Co</p>
